NEW_SUBSECTION = r"""
\subsection{Role of the resonance-aware decomposition and the equilibrium residual}
\label{subsec:results_ablation_summary}

The controlled ablation isolates the two methodological components: the modal-rational branch and the RBF-FD equilibrium residual, with the full table and figure collected in Appendix~\ref{app:ablation}.  The results show a clear division of responsibility.  Without the rational branch, a smooth neural background represents the resonance-dominated family poorly; adding the equilibrium residual improves the full-field fit of these pole-free variants while keeping peak locations essentially unchanged.  Once the exact pole branch is present, the resonance-sensitive part of the response is already resolved, and the additional physics increment on the complete model is small.  The ablation therefore confirms the design rationale of Section~\ref{subsec:rbffd_informed_surrogate}: the modal-rational representation is the mechanism that preserves parameter-dependent resonance locations, while the equilibrium residual acts as a background and full-field regularizer.
"""


